window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-f6ac5a281ec17982"]={"key":"ny_c-f6ac5a281ec17982","group":"ny_c","uid":"f6ac5a281ec17982","rank":4,"title":"tallow creek btam screening standard","occupation":"police_detective_supervisors","archetype":"supplied_source","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Sgt. Estelle Zalewski with Tallow Creek Community College Police. Dean Eamon Merriweather needs one usable behavioral threat assessment and management screening and referral standard before the second campus opens in January. Bellhaven Partners assembled the working material in `Tallow_Creek_BTAM_source.xlsx`; it combines excerpts and draft provisions associated with the state school-safety center, Cavendish Bureau, the county crisis team, and the college conduct code, but it was never reconciled into an operating document. Create `Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx` in the top level of the working directory where you started, using exactly that filename.\n\nThe workbook is for the two-campus BTAM team and must be usable by Frida Crowther and Dmitri Kaczmarek when they receive a concern, by Nils Ferreira when a clinical response may be appropriate, and by campus police when a matter may require police action. Build one concise screening and referral standard from the supplied material. Number the operating requirements within the workbook so a reviewer can follow them. Include the purpose and scope, the people or roles responsible for initial screening and escalation, the information to capture, a clearly defined tier structure, the trigger or decision basis for each tier, the action and referral that each tier starts, documentation and follow-up expectations, and a short section explaining how the standard applies across both campuses.\n\nThe four source voices do not use the same thresholds or vocabulary. Preserve the important source facts and identify their sources, but reconcile overlapping provisions into a coherent standard rather than pasting four separate policies together. Where the materials disagree about when a concern is a police matter rather than a clinical referral to Nils Ferreira, state the governing choice plainly and give a brief rationale grounded in the supplied material. Do not present a diagnosis, promise confidentiality, or create a new legal duty that the sources do not support. If a source provision cannot be reconciled confidently, show the uncertainty and identify who must make the decision rather than silently choosing an unsupported fact.\n\nMake the finished workbook easy to audit: include a source or crosswalk area linking substantive requirements to their originating material, a short implementation note for supervisors, and a compact decision aid that someone can use while screening. Keep the prose operational and avoid academic background. Do not copy the unrelated material in the source workbook into the standard, do not rely on any retired or helper field when interpreting the draft, and do not repeat a duplicated provision as if it were two separate requirements. Keep the source workbook unchanged; do not add invented people, campuses, agencies, contact details, thresholds, forms, or codes. Use only the names and organisations supplied in the brief or the source file. The result should be complete enough for oversight review while remaining practical for a first-line supervisor to run before January.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/Tallow_Creek_BTAM_source.xlsx` — Single supplied source workbook containing the partially completed BTAM draft and the source provisions that must be faithfully extracted, attributed, reconciled, and converted into the requested standard.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx` — A single spreadsheet containing the completed two-campus BTAM screening and referral standard, its operational decision aid, source crosswalk, and implementation note. (Write the file into the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; Keep the supplied source workbook unchanged.; Use only facts supported by the supplied workbook and the names and organisations in the brief.; The standard must be readable in spreadsheet form and suitable for oversight review.; Do not reproduce the unrelated adjacent table or use the retired helper field as authority.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/Tallow_Creek_BTAM_source.xlsx","bytes":7385,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/2cca78e3ffc620f6dcb80c01031150b4cecdb93e56751d76143a1a11ab590e21.xlsx","sha256":"2cca78e3ffc620f6dcb80c01031150b4cecdb93e56751d76143a1a11ab590e21","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Working material","row_count":21,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Bellhaven Partners | Tallow Creek BTAM working material","","","","","","","Records administration inventory"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Compiled 11/18/2025 - working draft excerpts"]},{"r":"4","cells":["Provision key","Source group","Topic","Draft provision","Retired helper - do not use","","","File box","Archive status\n(legacy)","Owner initials","Last scan","Retention shelf"]},{"r":"5","cells":["SSSC-01","State School-Safety Center","Purpose and scope","Use a behavioral threat assessment and management process to identify, assess, manage, and refer concerning behavior. The process is prevention-focused and applies to school settings.","High","","","ADM-14","active","BC","10/31/2025","S-2"]},{"r":"6","cells":["SSSC-02","State School-Safety Center","Intake information","Capture the report source, observed behavior or communication, people or setting affected, timing, and available supporting information. Record facts and distinguish them from speculation.","Routine","","","ADM-22","review","RM","11/02/2025","S-4"]},{"r":"7","cells":["SSSC-03","State School-Safety Center","Screening","Initial screening separates information that indicates immediate safety concern, information needing further assessment, and information that can be managed with support and monitoring. Do not use the screen to diagnose.","Clinical","","","ADM-31","hold","BC","11/07/2025","S-1"]},{"r":"8","cells":["SSSC-04","State School-Safety Center","Management","A concern may be reassessed when new information is received. Threat assessment and management are continuing processes, not a one-time label.","Closed"]},{"r":"9","cells":["SSSC-05","State School-Safety Center","Team review","Use a multidisciplinary threat assessment and management review to coordinate assessment, management, and referral when the initial screen indicates a concern needs further review.","Police"]},{"r":"10","cells":["CB-01","Cavendish Bureau","Report record","Record what was reported, who provided it, when it occurred or was received, the person or location involved, and available messages, images, or other supporting material.","Low"]},{"r":"11","cells":["CB-02","Cavendish Bureau","Urgent response","When reported behavior or information indicates an immediate or ongoing safety threat, seek a campus police response and escalate for urgent review. Preserve the reported information and document the action taken.","Clinical"]},{"r":"12","cells":["CB-03","Cavendish Bureau","Police boundary","A law-enforcement response is appropriate for an immediate or ongoing safety threat or information requiring police action; it is not the default response to every concerning behavior.","Routine"]},{"r":"13","cells":["CB-04","Cavendish Bureau","Documentation","Document the concern, screening decision, rationale, action, and referral or review path.","Urgent"]},{"r":"14","cells":["CB-04","Cavendish Bureau","Documentation","Document the concern, screening decision, rationale, action, and referral or review path.","Clinical"]},{"r":"15","cells":["CCT-01","County Crisis Team","Clinical intake","For a clinical referral, provide observed concerns, relevant timing, current setting or location when known, available supporting information, and the reason a clinical response may be appropriate.","Police"]},{"r":"16","cells":["CCT-02","County Crisis Team","Clinical boundary","Crisis-team intake may be appropriate when reported behavior suggests distress or a need for clinical assessment and the available information does not indicate an immediate or ongoing safety threat requiring police action.","Urgent"]},{"r":"17","cells":["CCT-03","County Crisis Team","Information gap","If intake information is incomplete, obtain available clarifying information and identify the responsible reviewer before relying on a clinical referral decision.","Closed"]},{"r":"18","cells":["TCCC-01","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","Conduct distinction","A behavioral threat assessment is not a disciplinary finding. Conduct-code review, if warranted by reported behavior, is separate from the assessment and management process.","Police"]},{"r":"19","cells":["TCCC-02","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","Conduct response","Reported conduct may be referred for conduct-code review based on the information available. A conduct-code implication does not by itself require a police response.","Urgent"]},{"r":"20","cells":["TCCC-03","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","Applicability","The conduct code applies to College activities and premises. Apply the same behavioral assessment and management approach wherever the concern is received.","Low"]},{"r":"21","cells":[]},{"r":"22","cells":["Draft notes: reconcile source language before use."]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx","bytes":14728,"extension":".xlsx","url":"assets/e0c0b998f2b76a8e0ef846140d907bc793d8bc9eccd08cddbe3a73a6a3407989.xlsx","sha256":"e0c0b998f2b76a8e0ef846140d907bc793d8bc9eccd08cddbe3a73a6a3407989","preview":{"kind":"sheets","sheets":[{"name":"Standard","row_count":30,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Tallow Creek Community College Police"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Behavioral Threat Assessment and Management (BTAM) Screening and Referral Standard | two-campus use | Owner: Sgt. Estelle Zalewski | Sponsor: Dean Eamon Merriweather"]},{"r":"4","cells":["1. Purpose and scope"]},{"r":"5","cells":["1.1","Purpose","Use this standard to receive, screen, assess, manage, and refer concerning behavior in a prevention-focused process. It is not a general student-conduct policy.","State School-Safety Center; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["1.2","Scope","This standard applies across both campuses whenever a concern is received. Behavioral threat assessment is not a disciplinary finding; a conduct-code review may proceed separately when warranted by reported behavior.","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["1.3","Screening rule","Use observable behavior, communications, and available information. Record what is known and what remains unverified; do not diagnose or treat speculation as fact.","State School-Safety Center","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["2. Roles and initial screen"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Req.","Role / point","Operating responsibility","Source basis","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["2.1","Frida Crowther and Dmitri Kaczmarek","When either receives a concern, initiate the initial screen using the compact decision aid and document the observed information, tier, basis, and disposition.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"12","cells":["2.2","BTAM team","Review and coordinate assessment, management, referral, and reassessment when the screen indicates further review or the available information does not support a confident tier decision.","State School-Safety Center; County Crisis Team","",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["2.3","Campus police","Provide the police response and urgent escalation path when the screen identifies an immediate or ongoing safety threat or information requiring police action.","Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["2.4","Nils Ferreira","Receive a clinical referral when observed information suggests distress or a need for clinical assessment and does not indicate an immediate or ongoing safety threat requiring police action.","County Crisis Team","",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["3. Intake and screening requirements"]},{"r":"17","cells":["Req.","Capture / do","Operational instruction","Source basis","",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["3.1","Record the concern","Capture what was reported or observed, who provided it, the person or setting affected, timing (occurred or received), and available messages, images, or other supporting material.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"19","cells":["3.2","Separate facts","Identify observed behavior or communication separately from inferences, missing facts, or speculation. A screen is not a diagnosis.","State School-Safety Center","",""]},{"r":"20","cells":["3.3","Screen and document","Assign the tier using the observable decision basis below, then document the screening decision, rationale, action, and referral, review, or monitoring path.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"22","cells":["4. Tier structure and referral path"]},{"r":"23","cells":["Tier","Observable decision basis / trigger","Immediate action","Referral, review, or monitoring path","Source basis",""]},{"r":"24","cells":["Tier 1 - Support / monitor","Information does not indicate an immediate or ongoing safety threat and can be managed with support and monitoring on the information available.","Document the disposition and any support or monitoring action; do not automatically refer to campus police.","Retain for monitoring and reassess if new information is received. Conduct-code review may be considered separately when warranted.","State School-Safety Center; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","E2F0D9"]},{"r":"25","cells":["Tier 2 - Further review / clinical","Information needs further assessment, or observed information suggests distress or a need for clinical assessment, but does not indicate an immediate or ongoing safety threat requiring police action.","Document the facts, information gap, and preliminary rationale. Obtain available clarifying information.","Refer the clinical intake information to Nils Ferreira; BTAM team coordinates review and reassesses as information is received.","State School-Safety Center; County Crisis Team","FFF2CC"]},{"r":"26","cells":["Tier 3 - Urgent police / BTAM","Reported behavior or information indicates an immediate or ongoing safety threat, or information requires police action.","Seek campus police response, preserve reported information, and document action taken; escalate for urgent BTAM review.","Campus police response and urgent BTAM review. Reassess management and referral needs as information is received.","Cavendish Bureau; State School-Safety Center","FCE4D6"]},{"r":"28","cells":["5. Police versus clinical referral; uncertainty"]},{"r":"29","cells":["5.1","Governing choice","Cavendish Bureau governs the police threshold: an immediate or ongoing safety threat, or information requiring police action, starts the campus-police path. County Crisis Team governs clinical intake only when observed information suggests a clinical need and does not indicate that police threshold.","Cavendish Bureau; County Crisis Team","",""]},{"r":"30","cells":["5.2","Rationale","This follows Cavendish Bureau’s direct police boundary while preserving County Crisis Team’s clinical-intake condition. Conduct-code implications alone do not require police action.","Cavendish Bureau; County Crisis Team; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","",""]},{"r":"31","cells":["5.3","Insufficient information","Do not force a tier. Record the missing information, obtain available clarification, and identify the BTAM team for review before relying on a clinical referral decision. Escalate to Tier 3 when the information indicates the urgent trigger.","County Crisis Team; Cavendish Bureau; State School-Safety Center","",""]},{"r":"33","cells":["6. Documentation, follow-up, and two-campus implementation"]},{"r":"34","cells":["6.1","Case record","Document the concern; report source; observed information; affected person or setting; timing; available supporting material; tier; rationale; immediate action; and referral, review, or monitoring path.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"35","cells":["6.2","Follow-up","BTAM team tracks Tier 2 and Tier 3 management and reassesses when new information is received. Tier 1 dispositions are revisited when new information changes the screening basis.","State School-Safety Center","",""]},{"r":"36","cells":["6.3","Supervisor implementation","Supervisors at both campuses use the same intake fields, tier definitions, and decision aid; check that the documented rationale matches the tier and route. Escalation is based on observed information, not campus location.","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code; State School-Safety Center","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Decision aid","row_count":16,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["BTAM Screening Decision Aid"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Use with the Standard. Record the decision and its observable basis; do not diagnose."]},{"r":"4","cells":["A. Capture before selecting a path"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Check","Capture","What to write","Source basis","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["A1","Report and source","What was reported or observed, and who provided it.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["A2","Affected person or setting","Person, location, or setting affected by the concern.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"8","cells":["A3","Timing and support","When it occurred or was received; available messages, images, or other supporting material.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["A4","Facts and gaps","Observed behavior or communication; separate unknowns and speculation. Do not diagnose.","State School-Safety Center","",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["B. Select the highest supported path"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Question","Yes - use this path","Immediate action","Next path / record","Source basis",""]},{"r":"13","cells":["Does the information indicate an immediate or ongoing safety threat, or require police action?","Tier 3 - Urgent police / BTAM","Seek campus police response; preserve reported information; document action; urgent BTAM review.","Record Tier 3, observed basis, and urgent action. Reassess as information is received.","Cavendish Bureau; State School-Safety Center",""]},{"r":"14","cells":["If no: does observed information suggest distress or a need for clinical assessment, or need further assessment?","Tier 2 - Further review / clinical","Document facts and gaps; obtain available clarification.","Refer clinical intake information to Nils Ferreira; BTAM team reviews and reassesses.","County Crisis Team; State School-Safety Center",""]},{"r":"15","cells":["If no: can it be managed with support and monitoring on the available information?","Tier 1 - Support / monitor","Document disposition and support or monitoring action.","Monitor; reassess with new information. Consider separate conduct-code review when warranted; no automatic police referral.","State School-Safety Center; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code",""]},{"r":"16","cells":["Is the information insufficient for a confident choice?","Hold tier; BTAM team review","Record missing information and obtain available clarification.","Identify BTAM team for review before relying on a clinical referral decision; move to Tier 3 if urgent trigger is indicated.","County Crisis Team; Cavendish Bureau; State School-Safety Center",""]},{"r":"18","cells":["C. Boundary reminder"]},{"r":"19","cells":["C1","Police vs. clinical","Cavendish Bureau governs the police threshold. County Crisis Team governs clinical intake only where the police threshold is not indicated. A conduct-code implication alone does not require police action.","Cavendish Bureau; County Crisis Team; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","",""]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Source crosswalk","row_count":16,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Source Crosswalk and Method Note"]},{"r":"2","cells":["Traceability for substantive operating requirements. Source wording was consolidated into one operating standard."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Method note"]},{"r":"5","cells":["M1","Scope of interpretation","The gold-standard derivation used substantive source columns Provision key, Source group, Topic, and Draft provision. The “Retired helper - do not use” field was excluded from interpretation and did not control any tier, threshold, or referral outcome.","","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["M2","Duplicate treatment","The two CB-04 rows have the same provision key and identical documentation provision. They were consolidated as one operational requirement and are not counted twice.","","",""]},{"r":"7","cells":["M3","Adjacent table","The separate Records administration inventory, including its legacy archive-status header, is unrelated to BTAM and is excluded from this crosswalk and standard.","","",""]},{"r":"9","cells":["Requirement-to-source crosswalk"]},{"r":"10","cells":["Standard requirement(s)","Operating treatment","Source key(s)","Originating material","Source provision summary",""]},{"r":"11","cells":["1.1","Prevention-focused screening, assessment, management, and referral; not conduct policy.","SSSC-01; TCCC-01","State School-Safety Center; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","BTAM purpose; assessment is not a disciplinary finding."]},{"r":"12","cells":["1.2; 6.3","Same standard across College activities and premises, expressly for both campuses.","TCCC-03","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","Applicability and common approach."]},{"r":"13","cells":["1.3; 3.1-3.2; A1-A4","Capture source, observations, affected setting, timing, support; distinguish facts from speculation; no diagnosis.","SSSC-02; SSSC-03; CB-01","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau","Intake facts and non-diagnostic screen."]},{"r":"14","cells":["2.2; 5.3; 6.2","BTAM review, management, clarification, and reassessment.","SSSC-04; SSSC-05; CCT-03","State School-Safety Center; County Crisis Team","Multidisciplinary review, continuing management, incomplete intake."]},{"r":"15","cells":["2.3; Tier 3; 5.1","Campus-police urgent path for immediate/ongoing threat or police-action information.","CB-02; CB-03","Cavendish Bureau","Urgent response and law-enforcement boundary."]},{"r":"16","cells":["2.4; Tier 2; 5.1","Clinical intake to Nils Ferreira when clinical need is suggested without police trigger.","CCT-01; CCT-02; CCT-03","County Crisis Team","Clinical intake criteria and information gap handling."]},{"r":"17","cells":["3.3; 6.1","Document concern, decision, rationale, action, and route once.","CB-04 (two duplicate source rows)","Cavendish Bureau","Duplicate keyed documentation provision consolidated once."]},{"r":"18","cells":["Tier 1; 1.2; 5.2","Routine support/monitoring and separate conduct-code consideration; no automatic police action.","SSSC-03; SSSC-04; TCCC-01; TCCC-02","State School-Safety Center; Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code","Routine screening distinction and conduct-code restraint."]}],"truncated":false},{"name":"Implementation note","row_count":11,"rows":[{"r":"1","cells":["Supervisor Implementation Note"]},{"r":"2","cells":["For consistent first-line screening before the second-campus opening."]},{"r":"4","cells":["Supervisor use"]},{"r":"5","cells":["Step","Supervisor direction","Why it matters","Source basis","",""]},{"r":"6","cells":["I1","Use the Standard and Decision aid at either campus whenever Frida Crowther or Dmitri Kaczmarek receives a concern.","A common intake and tier structure keeps campus location from changing the screening basis.","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code; State School-Safety Center"]},{"r":"7","cells":["I2","Check that the record contains observable information, source, affected person or setting, timing, supporting information, tier, rationale, action, and route.","This permits oversight reconstruction of the decision without a diagnosis or unsupported inference.","State School-Safety Center; Cavendish Bureau"]},{"r":"8","cells":["I3","Check escalation against the governing boundary: urgent police path for the Cavendish Bureau trigger; clinical intake to Nils Ferreira only where that trigger is not indicated.","The review uses the source with the direct police boundary and retains the County Crisis Team clinical condition.","Cavendish Bureau; County Crisis Team"]},{"r":"9","cells":["I4","Assign BTAM team review for Tier 2, Tier 3, and an insufficient-information screen; revisit a disposition when new information is received.","Management and reassessment continue after initial screening.","State School-Safety Center; County Crisis Team"]},{"r":"10","cells":["I5","Keep conduct-code review distinct from BTAM screening. A conduct implication can be considered separately but does not itself require police action.","This preserves the conduct-code distinction and proportionate routing.","Tallow Creek Community College Conduct Code"]},{"r":"12","cells":["Review checkpoint"]},{"r":"13","cells":["I6","Before closing a screening step","Confirm that the tier shown in the case record matches the Decision aid outcome and that the action, referral/review, and follow-up match that tier.","","",""]}],"truncated":false}],"note":"值与公式提取，不还原原始排版；每表最多120行、30列。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted workbook opens successfully as a valid spreadsheet.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook file","grader_hint":"Open with a standard spreadsheet library or office application."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered file is named Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filename","grader_hint":"Inspect the submitted filename."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook presents one integrated BTAM screening and referral standard rather than four unedited source excerpts.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook and extracted text","grader_hint":"Judge whether the artifact has a coherent operating sequence and consolidated provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard identifies Tallow Creek Community College Police as the operating context.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standard text","grader_hint":"Search extracted workbook text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard expressly covers both campuses.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope or implementation text","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit two-campus scope, not merely an incidental mention."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The scope and purpose accurately reflect screening, threat assessment, management, and referral without changing the work into a general student-conduct policy.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Purpose and scope","grader_hint":"Compare the stated purpose with the supplied draft and requested artifact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every substantive source provision used in the standard is traceable to an originating source in the workbook crosswalk or equivalent attribution.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source crosswalk","grader_hint":"Sample all major requirements and verify source labels and matching source text."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The crosswalk includes the state school-safety center material.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Crosswalk","grader_hint":"Verify the source name and linked provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The crosswalk includes Cavendish Bureau material.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Crosswalk","grader_hint":"Verify the source name and linked provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The crosswalk includes county crisis-team intake material.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Crosswalk","grader_hint":"Verify the source name and linked provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The crosswalk includes the college conduct code material.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Crosswalk","grader_hint":"Verify the source name and linked provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard identifies who receives or initiates a concern and who performs the initial screen.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roles section and decision aid","grader_hint":"Look for an actionable role assignment rather than only naming the team."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard assigns a distinct escalation or review responsibility to an appropriate role or team.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roles and escalation section","grader_hint":"Check that escalation ownership is explicit and not left to an unnamed person."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact uses the supplied name Nils Ferreira in the clinical referral context where applicable.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Referral section","grader_hint":"Search extracted text and verify the context is clinical referral, not an invented title."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The screening intake captures enough information to identify the concern, source, affected person or setting, timing, and available supporting information as required by the source material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Screening fields or decision aid","grader_hint":"Review the intake fields against the source provisions; do not require a particular layout."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard distinguishes observed behavior or information from unsupported diagnosis or speculation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Screening instructions","grader_hint":"Look for behavior-based wording and an instruction not to diagnose."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard contains multiple operational tiers that are defined by observable decision criteria rather than labels alone.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tier table","grader_hint":"Confirm that each tier has a meaning or threshold a screener can apply."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each defined tier has an associated immediate action.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tier table","grader_hint":"Check tier-by-tier for an action, not merely a general statement elsewhere."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Each defined tier has an associated referral, review, or monitoring path.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tier and referral sections","grader_hint":"Verify that every tier resolves to a responsible path."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The lowest or routine tier has a documented disposition that does not automatically escalate every concern to police.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tier table","grader_hint":"Judge whether the lowest tier is operationally meaningful and proportionate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The highest or urgent tier has a clearly stated urgent response and escalation path.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Tier table and decision aid","grader_hint":"Confirm that urgency is translated into a concrete response."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard states which source governs when deciding whether a concern is a police matter rather than a clinical referral to Nils Ferreira.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conflict-resolution or referral section","grader_hint":"Require an explicit source-governance statement, not an implication."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The police-versus-clinical boundary is defensible, understandable to a first-line supervisor, and grounded in the supplied materials.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Referral section and crosswalk","grader_hint":"Assess whether the tradeoff is reasoned without inventing law, diagnosis, or unsupported authority."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard identifies what happens when the available information is insufficient for a confident tier decision.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision aid or uncertainty section","grader_hint":"Look for a documented escalation, consultation, or follow-up treatment of uncertainty."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard preserves the source distinction between a threat or concern assessment and a disciplinary finding.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Definitions and scope","grader_hint":"Compare the wording with the conduct-code provisions in the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Conduct-code implications are represented accurately and are not converted into unsupported automatic police actions.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Conduct and referral sections","grader_hint":"Check both fidelity to the conduct code and restraint in escalation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Crisis-team intake criteria are reflected in the clinical referral decision or referral information requirements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Clinical referral section and crosswalk","grader_hint":"Match the artifact to the supplied crisis-team criteria."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Cavendish Bureau provisions are not presented as if they were college-specific facts without attribution or adaptation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Crosswalk and standard wording","grader_hint":"Look for source attribution and sensible contextual adaptation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard includes documentation expectations for the screening decision and its rationale.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Documentation section","grader_hint":"Require fields or instructions for recording basis and disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The standard includes follow-up, review, or reassessment expectations where the source material calls for continuing management.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Follow-up section","grader_hint":"Check that ongoing cases do not end at the initial tier assignment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The implementation note identifies how supervisors should use the standard consistently across the two campuses.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Implementation note","grader_hint":"Judge whether it provides practical supervisory guidance grounded in the source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The decision aid reflects the same tier definitions and referral outcomes as the main standard.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision aid compared with tier table","grader_hint":"Audit each decision path for internal agreement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The source duplicate or overlapping provision is represented once in the operational standard rather than counted as two separate requirements.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standard and crosswalk","grader_hint":"Use the source key to identify the seeded duplicate and check consolidation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The duplicate-key treatment is disclosed in the crosswalk, method note, or equivalent provenance note.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Provenance note","grader_hint":"Require an explicit statement that overlapping duplicate source rows were de-duplicated."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The retired helper column is not used as an independent requirement, threshold, or authoritative classification.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standard compared with source","grader_hint":"Compare classifications and thresholds against the substantive source fields, not the stale helper values."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The artifact discloses that the retired helper field was excluded from interpretation or otherwise makes that treatment auditable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Method or provenance note","grader_hint":"Look for a direct statement about the retired field."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The unrelated adjacent table is excluded from the standard's substantive content and source crosswalk.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Delivered workbook compared with source geometry","grader_hint":"Identify the side table by its distinct subject and verify that its records are not copied as BTAM provisions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The line break embedded in the unrelated table's header does not create a spurious BTAM field or requirement in the output.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Extracted workbook text","grader_hint":"Search for the side-table header and inspect output headers."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"No unsupported person, agency, campus, contact detail, code, deadline, or legal obligation is invented.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire workbook compared with brief and source","grader_hint":"Flag additions that cannot be traced to the brief or source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The supplied names used in the workbook remain consistent and are not misspelled or assigned unsupported roles.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Entire workbook","grader_hint":"Check Estelle Zalewski, Frida Crowther, Dmitri Kaczmarek, Eamon Merriweather, and Nils Ferreira against the brief and source."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The workbook is sufficiently clear and compact that a supervisor can use it during screening and an oversight reviewer can reconstruct the decision logic.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered workbook","grader_hint":"Judge readability, navigability, operational clarity, and auditability together."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The workbook contains the requested purpose and scope, roles, intake information, tier definitions, tier triggers, tier actions, referrals, documentation, follow-up, two-campus implementation note, source crosswalk, and decision aid.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook contents","grader_hint":"Walk the artifact against each requested component; award only when each is materially present."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The delivered workbook contains no #REF!, #DIV/0!, or #VALUE! errors.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Workbook cell values and formulas","grader_hint":"Inspect formulas and displayed values across all sheets."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The supplied source workbook remains unchanged from the provided file.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Working-directory source workbook","grader_hint":"Compare file hash or cell-level content with the supplied source."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Tallow Creek Community College is preparing its police department and threat assessment team for the opening of a second campus. Sgt. Estelle Zalewski is responsible for turning a fragmented draft into a standard that can be used consistently by campus personnel, clinicians, and police supervisors.","difficulty_sources":["The supplied draft combines guidance from four institutions with different scopes and does not resolve their overlaps.","The practitioner must turn narrative provisions into usable screening tiers and referral actions without inventing unsupported requirements.","The source contains duplicate keyed provisions, a stale retired helper column, and an unrelated adjacent table that must not be mistaken for source content."],"authoring_plan":{"source_file":{"filename":"Tallow_Creek_BTAM_source.xlsx","semantic_content":"Create one spreadsheet containing a partially completed BTAM draft assembled from four clearly attributed source groups: a state school-safety center guide, Cavendish Bureau model policy, county crisis-team intake criteria, and the Tallow Creek Community College conduct code. The substantive material must cover purpose and scope, observable concern intake, screening roles, tier concepts or criteria, police and clinical referral boundaries, documentation, follow-up, and campus applicability. Include enough overlapping and differently scoped prose that the worker must reconcile it into one standard. Use the supplied people and organisations where roles are needed: Estelle Zalewski, Frida Crowther, Dmitri Kaczmarek, Eamon Merriweather, and Nils Ferreira; Bellhaven Partners may appear as the assembling firm.","defects":[{"type":"duplicate_or_overlapping_rows","construction":"In the substantive main table, include two or more rows with the same source-defined provision key and materially overlapping content. The key must be visible in the source itself and the duplicate must be recognizable as an overlap, not a typo. The duplicate should concern an operational BTAM requirement that belongs once in the final standard."},{"type":"retired_helper_column","construction":"Include a clearly labeled retired/helper column adjacent to the substantive fields. Populate it with stale classifications that conflict with at least some current substantive source text. The source must visibly indicate that the field is retired or helper-only, but must not provide a replacement rule beyond the substantive fields."},{"type":"unrelated_adjacent_table","construction":"Place a separate, unrelated table beside the substantive BTAM table on the same worksheet. Give it a different subject, such as internal document administration, and include a header string containing an embedded line break. It must be distinguishable by its title and fields so a careful worker can exclude it."}],"exclusions":"Do not seed any other standard defect: no formula errors, broken references, missing-value trap, malformed dates, inconsistent numeric units, hidden image-only facts, or additional unrelated tables. Do not resolve the substantive policy conflicts in the source."},"transformation":"The solver must lightly edit and reshape the supplied narrative provisions into a new operational spreadsheet standard. The final artifact should consolidate duplicate keyed provisions, ignore the retired helper field, exclude the adjacent unrelated table, preserve material source facts with attribution, and make a defensible explicit choice about the police-versus-clinical boundary. The request asks for the components but does not dictate the tier names, exact layout, or unsupported local procedure.","gold_rules":["Every substantive requirement in the final standard must be traceable to one of the four source groups or to the supplied brief.","The duplicate key represents one requirement, so it must not generate two operational requirements.","The retired helper column is stale and cannot control a tier, threshold, or referral outcome.","The adjacent table and its line-break header are unrelated and must not appear as BTAM content.","The final standard must preserve the source distinction between behavioral threat assessment, clinical referral, conduct response, and police action while explicitly reconciling their boundary.","The grader should accept different tier labels and layouts when the observable criteria, actions, referrals, documentation, and source rationale are substantively equivalent.","The final workbook must contain a practical decision aid, source crosswalk, and implementation note, with internal agreement among those elements."],"review_method":"Build the source workbook with ordinary text cells and formulas only as needed, then create an independent reference standard from the specified semantic rules. Walk every rubric item against the reference workbook, checking source fidelity, explicit defect treatment, operational completeness, internal consistency, and rendered usability. Confirm that no rubric item depends on an unstated literal value or internet fact."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"btam_source_workbook","filename":"Tallow_Creek_BTAM_source.xlsx","purpose":"Single supplied source workbook containing the partially completed BTAM draft and the source provisions that must be faithfully extracted, attributed, reconciled, and converted into the requested standard.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the workbook from the top level of the working directory. The substantive draft is the main table; a separate table appears beside it on the same sheet."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"btam_standard_workbook","filename":"Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet","description":"A single spreadsheet containing the completed two-campus BTAM screening and referral standard, its operational decision aid, source crosswalk, and implementation note.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","Keep the supplied source workbook unchanged.","Use only facts supported by the supplied workbook and the names and organisations in the brief.","The standard must be readable in spreadsheet form and suitable for oversight review.","Do not reproduce the unrelated adjacent table or use the retired helper field as authority."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"inspect_quality","work_product":"investigation_casefile","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"supplied_source@v4","occupation":"police_detective_supervisors","sector":"government","task_archetype":"supplied_source","estimated_professional_hours":4.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have an independent reviewer compare the delivered standard with the supplied workbook, verify source traceability and defect handling, then judge whether the resulting tier and referral logic is operationally defensible.","minimum_reviewers":1,"known_limitations":["The supplied material is intentionally institutionally heterogeneous, so more than one defensible reconciliation may satisfy the judgement criteria.","The grader should not require a particular sheet layout or invented local terminology beyond the names and source labels present in the brief or workbook."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:34:01+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:34:01+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:34:01+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:34:01+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R22']","checked_at":"2026-08-25T08:34:01+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/f6ac5a281ec17982","declared_deliverables":["Tallow_Creek_BTAM_standard.xlsx"]};
